<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 19:30:59 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'Polarised Brazil': Lula remains a ‘strong candidate’ despite the challenges of incumbency</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260907-polarised-brazil-lula-remains-a-strong-candidate-despite-the-challenges-of-incumbency</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Andreza Aruska de Souza Santos, Director of King’s Brazil Institute at the School of Global Affairs, King’s College London and Associate Professor in Brazil and Latin American Studies. According to Aruska, Brazil’s approaching elections can be viewed through the following prism: macroeconomic performance and political confidence are moving on different tracks. While headline indicators may suggest an economy performing relatively well, she argues that many Brazilians experience a much harsher reality shaped by the cost of living and a volatile job market.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84f2ba22-aaea-11f1-8390-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10976096836a9f034d0eb2a8-89289314.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84f2ba22-aaea-11f1-8390-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-10976096836a9f034d0eb2a8-89289314.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d9f7a70-aaed-11f1-80d2-bb4ee502072c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:50:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Tunisians tell the story of their summer of shortages</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260907-tunisians-tell-story-their-summer-shortages</link><description>
Frequent water and power cuts, long queues for bottled water, poultry farms destroyed by the heat: these have been the scenes across Tunisia this summer as millions of people were affected by shortages in electricity and water. Our Observers say this is the result of years of underinvestment in infrastructure while the Tunisian president, for his part, blames "deliberate and planned acts of sabotage”. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd7419ca-a85d-11f1-8484-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-de-Matthew-Metro-sur-son-profil-Facebook-27.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd7419ca-a85d-11f1-8484-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-de-Matthew-Metro-sur-son-profil-Facebook-27.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b84e832-aadd-11f1-83c2-e38bbda28610</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:50:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bd7419ca-a85d-11f1-8484-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-de-Matthew-Metro-sur-son-profil-Facebook-27.png">© X / TikTok</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'What we see right now is that Putin has zero interest in ending the war', Ukrainian MP Yasko says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/what-we-see-right-now-is-that-putin-has-zero-interest-in-ending-the-war-ukrainian-mp-yasko-says</link><description>
US envoy Steve Witkoff on Monday touted progress in weekend discussions with Ukraine and Russia, raising the prospect of reviving three-way peace talks to end Europe's deadliest conflict since World War II. Ukrainian MP Lisa Yasko says that "we don't trust these talks", describing the US envoys' flattery towards Russian President Vladimir Putin as "disgraceful".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2931813c-aaea-11f1-a276-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-200740-201844-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2931813c-aaea-11f1-a276-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-200740-201844-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e57ec64-aaea-11f1-bdbe-4fa18040d678</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:38:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel warns of 'full-scale war' if Palestinian Authority launches Oct. 7-style attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israel-warns-of-full-scale-war-if-palestinian-authority-launches-oct-7-style-attack</link><description>
Israel on Monday threatened a “full-scale war” against the Palestinian Authority if it believed the West Bank-based body was preparing an attack on Israeli forces or settlements resembling Hamas’s October 7, 2023 assault. The warning was denounced by Palestinian authorities as an attempt to fuel the conflict during the Israeli election season.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a5ad172-aae3-11f1-86fb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6GC4RR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a5ad172-aae3-11f1-86fb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6GC4RR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">276750a0-aadd-11f1-973d-9175e80f4543</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:08:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8a5ad172-aae3-11f1-86fb-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6GC4RR.jpg">© Zain Jaafar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Eiffel Tower workers go on strike after female staff 'sidelined' for Hindu group's visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260907-strike-closes-eiffel-tower-paris-exclusion-female-staff-hindu-group-visit-baps</link><description>
The Eiffel Tower was forced to close on Monday after staff went on strike to protest the “sidelining” and “replacement” of female employees during a recent visit by a Hindu delegation. The Paris landmark's operator said the group had requested that the private visit be organised in such a way as to limit “interactions with women”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5eb8f834-aadc-11f1-8297-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C79B3WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5eb8f834-aadc-11f1-8297-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C79B3WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6883359a-aadd-11f1-a319-314d5c571bdf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 17:08:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5eb8f834-aadc-11f1-8297-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C79B3WE.jpg">© Kenzo Tribouillard, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Avalanche kills at least 11 climbers in southern Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-avalanche-kills-at-least-11-climbers-in-southern-russia</link><description>
⁠At least ​11 people were killed and six ​others injured after an avalanche struck a group of climbers in Russia's ​southern Kabardino-Balkaria ‌Republic, local emergency services said. The ‌avalanche swept down Mount Mizhirgi, ⁠one of the highest peaks in Russia's North Caucasus.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37b2dd78-aacc-11f1-ac97-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/miniaalane.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/37b2dd78-aacc-11f1-ac97-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/miniaalane.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e95feee-aacc-11f1-8328-2b49e65c2de6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 15:00:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Will AfD win in Germany boost France's far right?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-will-afd-win-in-germany-boost-france-s-far-right</link><description>
The Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday, exit polls showed, putting a far-right party on the cusp of power at state level for the first time since World War Two. The result has garnered attention across Europe, not least in France where national elections next year could see far-right veteran Marine Le Pen become president.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01d8ccb0-aac9-11f1-a974-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150749-151521-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/01d8ccb0-aac9-11f1-a974-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150749-151521-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06818996-aac9-11f1-bdfa-59784994219f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:38:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon kill 11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11</link><description>
Israeli strikes ⁠on a ​southern Lebanese town early on Monday killed at least 11 people including two children ​and two medics, Lebanon's state news agency said. Israel has intensified its bombardment of south Lebanon in recent days despite a June ceasefire that was meant ​to halt fighting ‌between the Israeli military and Lebanese armed ⁠group Hezbollah. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c410c12-aac3-11f1-ba63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minilebanon.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6c410c12-aac3-11f1-ba63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minilebanon.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76dbfbfa-aac3-11f1-b3a5-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:10:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Céline Dion and Jay-Z bring their hits to Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260907-c%C3%A9line-dion-and-jay-z-bring-their-hits-to-paris</link><description>
In this edition of our arts24 music show, Jennifer Ben Brahim brings us a roundup of some of the week's most anticipated Paris concerts. From Céline Dion kicking off her 16 sold-out shows at La Défense Arena, to American rapper Jay-Z celebrating his 30-year career at the Stade de France, we've got you covered. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c2fbf84-aabc-11f1-8cbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16249183416a9eb5a6428b35-31705991.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3c2fbf84-aabc-11f1-8cbe-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16249183416a9eb5a6428b35-31705991.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c584f06-aabd-11f1-98ec-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:05:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jennifer BEN BRAHIM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What now for Germany's Merz after AfD win?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-what-now-for-germany-s-merz-after-afd-win</link><description>
The far-right AfD's triumph in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt marks a defeat for German Chancellor Friedrich Merz and sends a warning to other European leaders battling the same mixture of slow growth and disillusion with mainstream politics. In an increasingly polarized political system, Merz, whose personal approval ratings have sunk ‌to record lows, was one of the main targets of voter ire over the cost of living, pensions and economic insecurity. France 24’s Philip Turle takes a look at what the AfD’s victory means for the German leader and for Europe.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89602e84-aac0-11f1-96ff-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-143117-143538-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/89602e84-aac0-11f1-96ff-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-143117-143538-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8eaab314-aac0-11f1-b490-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:01:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saxony-Anhalt poll: 'A huge blow for the CDU, but also a huge win for the AfD'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-saxony-anhalt-poll-a-huge-blow-for-the-cdu-but-also-a-huge-win-for-the-afd-1</link><description>
Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Markus Ziener, Visiting Senior Fellow at the German Marshall Fund. He interprets the AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt as a potentially historic turning point in post-war German politics. For Ziener, the significance lies not only in the scale of the far right’s electoral success, but also in the constituency behind it: many AfD voters, he argues, were previously politically disengaged rather than simply defecting from established parties. This complicates conventional explanations of the result as a straightforward transfer of support from the CDU to the AfD and raises a deeper question about the political expectations of a newly mobilised electorate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a1ef7e-aac2-11f1-ad2d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150057-150748-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3a1ef7e-aac2-11f1-ad2d-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-150057-150748-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a99d2b1e-aac2-11f1-b13f-39bbc4f04cbf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 14:01:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How far-right AfD breakthrough may ‘cause absolute chaos’ in Germany</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260907-how-far-right-breakthrough-may-cause-absolute-chaos-in-germany-afd</link><description>
Germany’s Alternative for Germany (AfD) came out well ahead in Sunday’s regional elections in the state of Saxony-Anhalt, becoming the first far-right party to come close to gaining power at the regional level since World War II. The lead candidate of the party in the state, Ulrich Siegmund, said Monday that his party had already initiated talks towards building a governing majority.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d78d6c00-aab8-11f1-8074-bb94302a716d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:45:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/99c5cf00-aa83-11f1-809d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26249706755348.jpg">© Matthias Schrader, AP</source><dc:creator>Simon FEISTHAUER FOURNET</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Two children among dead in Israeli strikes on Lebanon</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-two-children-among-dead-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon</link><description>
Israeli airstrikes overnight killed 11 people in a south Lebanon village, including two infants, Lebanese state media said Monday, a day after separate raids left seven dead. France 24's Renée Davis in Beirut has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d5282ce-aabc-11f1-a75a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-140744-141004-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9d5282ce-aabc-11f1-a75a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-140744-141004-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1d61ec8-aabc-11f1-86b4-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:20:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>REPLAY: 'Shocked' Merz speaks after far-right election victory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-replay-shocked-merz-speaks-after-far-right-election-victory</link><description>
German Chancellor Friedrich Merz said Monday he was "deeply shocked" after his centre-right party suffered a heavy loss in a state poll to the far-right AfD, but vowed to push on with reforms. Watch his press conference in full above.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/054a05d8-aabc-11f1-a1f6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-133511-135547-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/054a05d8-aabc-11f1-a1f6-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-133511-135547-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a7c5286-aabc-11f1-95f3-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:04:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Idiots and traitors’: World reacts to AfD’s election victory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-idiots-and-traitors-world-reacts-to-afd-s-election-victory</link><description>
The Alternative for Germany (AfD) surged into first place in state elections in Saxony-Anhalt on Sunday. The result puts a far-right party within reach of power at the state level for the first time in the country since World War II. The outcome has European capitals taking notice, particularly in France where the campaign for next year's presidential elections has gotten underway.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ddd35d8-aab8-11f1-8553-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120611-120807-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ddd35d8-aab8-11f1-8553-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120611-120807-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2272b848-aab8-11f1-98e4-bb94302a716d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 13:02:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>UN rapporteur says Israeli rubble-clearing in Gaza could erase 'atrocity crimes' evidence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence</link><description>
The United Nations Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese warned on Monday that the large-scale rubble removal in parts of Gaza under Israeli control could risk erasing "evidence relevant to the investigation of alleged international crimes". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d529b836-aaba-11f1-8535-e7288cd5752f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:51:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/22ab0c38-aac3-11f1-8592-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236599212384.jpg">© Jehad Alshrafi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'We’re all in crisis': Populist far-right 'trend' sweeping across Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-we-re-all-in-crisis-populist-far-right-trend-sweeping-across-europe-1</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome our international affairs editor, Philip Turle, and Sylvie Bermann, France's first female ambassador to three member countries of the United Nations Security Council: China, the United Kingdom and Russia. The AfD’s breakthrough in Saxony-Anhalt should be understood, according to Sylvie Bermann, as part of a wider transformation of European politics rather than as an isolated German electoral shock. Brexit and Donald Trump’s victories helped normalise political positions previously regarded as outside the governing mainstream, while successive economic and geopolitical crises have weakened confidence in established parties. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d5e75d2-aab6-11f1-bc26-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-130059-131732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2d5e75d2-aab6-11f1-bc26-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-130059-131732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33b23d92-aab6-11f1-9063-ff9d54eec782</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:41:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tech 24</category><title>Driverless taxi services are rolling out fast across the world</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20260907-driverless-taxi-services-are-rolling-out-fast-across-the-world</link><description>
From Austin to London, the current robotaxi boom is raising hard questions about safety and jobs. We take a closer look in this edition of Tech 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1903060c-aab6-11f1-aab3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6702827096a9eab5a21bcf2-98330213.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1903060c-aab6-11f1-aab3-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6702827096a9eab5a21bcf2-98330213.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">52170c8e-a9f5-11f1-9e31-9b447c8e7aa4</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:29:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charlotte Lam</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who could form a coalition with Germany's AfD after election victory?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-who-could-form-a-coalition-with-germany-s-afd-after-election-victory</link><description>
Germany's far-right AfD won a landslide victory in a key regional election Sunday in the ex-communist east, a result seen as a stinging rebuke for Chancellor Friedrich Merz, but looked set to miss out on an absolute majority to govern alone. The big question now is who, if anyone, will be willing to form a coalition with the party, says France 24's correspondent Nick Holdsworth.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b084944-aaa9-11f1-9300-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120156-120548-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9b084944-aaa9-11f1-9300-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260907-120156-120548-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a00a1760-aaa9-11f1-b7c0-11268430d064</guid><pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 12:23:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>'This might be the year': Mbappé embraces Ballon d'Or talk after World Cup exploits</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260907-this-might-be-the-year-mbapp%C3%A9-embraces-ballon-d-or-talk-after-world-cup-exploits</link><description>
Real Madrid star Kylian Mbappé played up his chances of the winning the Ballon d'Or this year after scoring 10 goals at the recent World Cup to become the tournament's all-time leading scorer. Nominees for the prestigious award will be unveiled on Tuesday.
